<%# Shown while staff still need to resolve this account's duplicate review -- either on arrival,
    before any work is done, or after a submission the server refused. Deliberately NOT the
    #error-summary block: the constituent made no error, nothing failed to save, and their draft is
    intact. So this is role="status" with a polite live region and no focus seizure, rather than an
    assertive alert that grabs focus. %>
<% if @pending_identity_review_message.present? %>
  <div id="pending-review-notice"
       class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 p-4 rounded mb-6 text-blue-900"
       role="status"
       aria-live="polite"
       aria-atomic="true">
    <p><%= @pending_identity_review_message %></p>
    <%# Only on the refusal path. A browser cannot repopulate a file input, so the documents this
        constituent selected are gone from the form -- and unlike their typed answers, nothing
        re-renders them. Saying so, with the one action that actually recovers them, is the
        difference between a lost upload and a two-click fix. Never shown on arrival, where there
        is nothing selected yet to have lost. %>
    <% if @pending_identity_review_documents_message.present? %>
      <p id="pending-review-documents-notice" class="mt-2">
        <%= @pending_identity_review_documents_message %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
